  "name": "playbook-evidence-activation-loop",
  "title": "Evidence-activate candidate playbooks after explicit exposure outcomes",
  "description": "Story 1 proved DONE experience can become an inert candidate playbook. The remaining product gap is that a candidate with explicit exposure and structured helped outcomes must be activatable by evidence, without asking a human to manually promote it or relying on a default-off sweep flag. This story makes the evidence-activation apply path write the needed recommendation evidence and activation audit atomically enough for user-facing CLI use, then proves active playbooks are consumed by runtime memory while DONE success alone remains insufficient.",
